>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_backend`

``` hol4
Refute.register_backend : backend -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds or replaces a Refute search backend.

``` hol4
type backend =
  {name : string,
   weight : int,
   configured : unit -> bool,
   requires : requirement,
   input : goal_form,
   run : config -> instance list -> outcome}
```

`run` returns `Counterexample` of a list of the records below,
`NoCounterexample`, or `Unknown` of diagnostic strings:

``` hol4
type model_report =
  {skolems : (string * term) list,
   consts : (term * string * term) list,
   types : (hol_type * term list * bool) list}

type counterexample =
  {backend : string, substrate : string, certainty : certainty,
   bindings : (term * term) list, evals : (term * term) list,
   cert : thm option, scope : (hol_type * int) list option,
   model : model_report option, stats : (string * int) list}
```

Registrations are session-local; a later backend with the same `name`
replaces the old one.  Eligible backends are ordered by increasing
`weight`, then name.  `configured` is queried when a search is
selected.  `requires` is `AnyGoal`, `ExecutableGoal`, or
`ExecutableGoalUnless predicate`, the last accepting a non-executable
goal when `predicate cfg instances` holds.  `input` requests
`MonoInstances` or `PolyOriginal` instances.

The backend gets the conservative certainty ceiling `Genuine`.  This is
safe for any backend, but a race then waits for it after a weaker
result from another backend; the built-in narrowing and model-finder
backends declare tighter ceilings.

Exceptions and ordinary timeouts in `run` become `Unknown`; interrupts
are re-raised.

### See also

[`Refute.config`](#Refute.config),
[`Refute.refute`](#Refute.refute)

The extension model is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
